---
/**
 * DifficultyChip — static difficulty label (design §6.5, site spec §8, §9).
 *
 * Props:
 * - `difficulty` "beginner" | "intermediate" — the WORD is the signal, so the
 *   chip stays neutral (no `--hl-*` hue spent; those six roles are reserved for
 *   the visualization, design-tokens-m1.md Decision 3). Because meaning is never
 *   carried by colour, monochrome, forced-colors and screen-reader renderings
 *   lose nothing (§12).
 *
 * Neutral pill: surface fill, 1px border, uppercase --text-xs, muted text.
 * `--text-muted` on `--surface` is 6.67:1 light / 7.22:1 dark, and 6.49:1 /
 * 7.80:1 where the chip sits directly on the canvas (the lesson meta row) — the
 * label clears 1.4.3 on both backdrops. The `--border` keyline is decorative and
 * owes no floor (1.36:1 on a card, 1.32:1 on the canvas), which is exactly the
 * point: nothing here competes with the algorithm state on a lesson page.
 * Reading only tokens is also what keeps the chip off the print sheet's problem
 * list: global.css's `@media print` block forces the light token set globally,
 * so a dark-theme print needs no component-local override here.
 *
 * M7.3 evaluated two ways to make the two "Intermediate" lessons findable among
 * the thirteen "Beginner" ones, and shipped NEITHER:
 * - Soft semantic fills (VD-6/CMP-2) — proposed, built, then REJECTED at design
 *   review, which withheld sign-off. Three reasons, all measured or structural:
 *   the fills are 1.05–1.21:1 against the card they actually sit on (1.03–1.30:1
 *   against the canvas — re-measured on the achromatic palette, which moved the
 *   canvas but not the white card), so they do almost no perceptual work; what separation
 *   remained was carried by the label hue alone, which is the colour-only
 *   channel the component exists to avoid leaning on; and painting all thirteen
 *   beginner chips as loudly as the two intermediate ones inverts the very
 *   Von Restorff argument the change was made from. Spec §8 permits this exact
 *   treatment but gates it on designer sign-off, and §19 keeps the whole
 *   question open — with sign-off withheld, the neutral treatment stands.
 * - Badge-the-exception (leave "Beginner" neutral, mark only "Intermediate") —
 *   still OPEN, not rejected. §8 enumerates the chip among the lesson card's
 *   elements and describes only the soft-fill variant, so this one needs a §8
 *   amendment as well as sign-off; it is not a bug fix to be slipped in.
 */
interface Props {
  difficulty: 'beginner' | 'intermediate';
}

const { difficulty } = Astro.props;
const label = difficulty[0]!.toUpperCase() + difficulty.slice(1);
---

<span class="difficulty-chip">{label}</span>

<style>
  .difficulty-chip {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--surface);
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-3);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
